DAY 25 — PENTEST METHODOLOGY (QUICK NOTES)

PENTEST WORKFLOW
Scope → Recon → Enumeration → Vulnerability Assessment → Exploitation → Evidence → Reporting

SCOPE
Defines what can/cannot be tested and keeps testing authorized.

RECON
Gather information about the target.

ENUMERATION
Actively identify:

Open ports
Services
Versions
Attack surface

VULNERABILITY ASSESSMENT
Determine whether identified services have security weaknesses before exploiting.

EXPLOITATION
Safely validate confirmed vulnerabilities in an authorized lab.

EVIDENCE
Record:

Timestamp
Commands
Tool output
Screenshots
Requests/responses
Finding details

TOOL MAP
Nmap → ports/services
Burp Suite → web requests
Wireshark → network packets
Metasploit → known lab vulnerabilities

KEY RULE
Open port ≠ vulnerability.
Identify → verify → test → document.
